# pyvenv.cfg records the absolute path of the interpreter the venv was built
# from, so a committed one carries whichever machine created it - this repo had
# one pinning C:\Users\SHAMBHAVI PATIL\...\Python311, which is meaningless on
# every other developer's machine.
pyvenv.cfg

# Editor / assistant state
# .cursor holds both throwaway logs and shared project rules, so it is ignored
# selectively: the rules are team policy and MUST stay tracked (the
# no-cursor-attribution rule keeps AI co-author trailers out of commits), while
# debug logs are per-session noise.
.cursor/*
!.cursor/rules/
.cursor/**/*.log
debug-*.log

